<h2>1. Who operates NeonLib</h2>
<p>NeonLib is an Android application provided by Web Solutions, obrt za informatičke usluge, vl. Goran Sambolić, operating under the Neon Break brand, Varaždinska ulica 11, Zlatar, Croatia. Croatian Craft Register: MBO 99052687. Contact for privacy questions and requests: <a href="mailto:info@neonbreak.com">info@neonbreak.com</a>.</p>
<p>This policy covers the Android application and its collection and reporting API. Website enquiries and publisher accounts are also covered by our <a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/privacy-policy/' ) ); ?>">website privacy policy</a>.</p>
<h2>2. Your documents and local AI</h2>
<p>Notes, imported documents, downloaded collections, conversation data and search indexes are stored in the app's local storage. Local search and downloaded local AI models process content on your device. Using these local features does not itself upload your document text to Neon Break.</p>
<p>Android backup and device-transfer services may copy eligible app data according to your device settings. Local storage does not exclude operating-system backups. Exported files and backups are managed separately from the app.</p>
<h2>3. Optional online AI</h2>
<p>If you configure and use an online AI provider, your question and relevant document passages are sent directly to that provider. Chat requests may also include conversation history. Your API key is used to authenticate requests to your selected provider and is stored by the app using Android Keystore-backed encryption.</p>
<p>The provider you choose may process data outside the European Economic Area and has its own privacy, retention and contractual terms. Review those terms before using online AI with personal or confidential information. You can choose local AI instead.</p>
<h2>4. Collections and downloads</h2>
<p>Our API receives requests for the collection catalogue, documents, updates and availability, including the requested collection identifiers. Model downloads connect to Hugging Face and its download infrastructure. These network services receive your IP address and technical request information needed to deliver their services.</p>
<h2>5. Reports and moderation</h2>
<p>When you submit a report, we receive the explanation you enter, a report identifier, the report type, and information identifying the reported answer, collection or publisher. A collection report may include its content version. An AI answer excerpt is sent only if you select the option to include it, and you can edit it before sending.</p>
<p>Authorized moderators use reports to investigate problems and record their resolution. Please include only the information needed to explain the issue. Our backend uses a keyed hash derived from your IP address to limit abusive submissions. Hosting systems may separately record technical access and security logs.</p>
<h2>6. Hosting, purposes and recipients</h2>
<p>The NeonLib API is hosted with Hetzner in Germany, within the European Union. Hosting and infrastructure providers process information necessary to operate and secure the service. Configuring an online AI service or downloading a model also connects you to the relevant provider described above. We may disclose information where required by law.</p>
<p>We process service requests to provide requested functionality, reports to investigate content issues, and technical information to protect availability and security. Applicable legal bases include performance of the requested service, legitimate interests in service security and content moderation, compliance with legal obligations, and consent where required. We do not sell personal data.</p>
<h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>Local app data remains until you remove it through the app or clear the app's storage in Android settings. Removing local data does not delete reports already submitted to our server. Backups, exported documents and data held by your selected online provider may require separate deletion.</p>
<p>Open reports are retained while they are being investigated. Our retention policy is to delete closed reports and associated personal moderation notes 90 days after closure, except when a legal obligation or an active dispute requires longer retention. This policy is currently administered manually; automatic scheduled deletion is not yet enabled.</p>
<p>Technical logs and backup copies are retained only for the operational, recovery or security purposes for which they are needed, or to meet legal obligations. They are restricted to those purposes and may expire separately from active records. Contact us for information about a specific record or a deletion request.</p>
<h2>8. Your rights and contact</h2>
<p><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/neonlib/delete-data/' ) ); ?>">Request deletion of NeonLib data</a></p>
<p>Where applicable under the GDPR, you may request access, correction, erasure, restriction or portability, and object to processing. Where processing relies on consent, you may withdraw it without affecting earlier lawful processing. Send requests to <a href="mailto:info@neonbreak.com">info@neonbreak.com</a>. Include a report identifier if available, without sending unnecessary sensitive information. We may need proportionate information to locate records and verify a request.</p>
<p>You may complain to the Croatian Personal Data Protection Agency (AZOP) or another competent supervisory authority.</p>
<h2>9. Adults and policy updates</h2>
<p>NeonLib is intended for adults aged 18 and over. Contact us if you believe a minor has provided personal information to our service. We will update this page when relevant processing practices change and revise the date above.</p>
